# Job environment for the Majadu one-shot units.
#
# Installed on the VPS as /srv/qouver/apps/majadu/env/majadu-job.env with mode
# 600 and owned by the deploy user.
#
# Why this file exists: majadu-janitor, majadu-snapshot and majadu-ingest load
# this file and nothing else. They connect as the application role and read no
# credential that can change the schema, read the staging copy or take a dump.
# Before this split they loaded majadu-tools.env, which also carries
# MAJADU_OWNER_DSN, MAJADU_ETL_DSN, MAJADU_ETL_SOURCE_DSN,
# MAJADU_BACKUP_DSN_BM2 and MAJADU_CUTOVER_RESTORE_DSN, so a compromised cron
# job held the owner role for a database that is the whole product.
#
# The API unit is the model this follows: majadu-api.container loads
# majadu-prod.env, which carries only what the request path reads.
#
# What is deliberately absent, and stays in majadu-tools.env:
#   MAJADU_OWNER_DSN            DDL and RLS bypass; migrations and operator tools
#   MAJADU_ETL_DSN              the cutover loader
#   MAJADU_ETL_SOURCE_DSN       reads bm_staging
#   MAJADU_BACKUP_DSN_BM2       dumps the database
#   MAJADU_CUTOVER_RESTORE_DSN  drops and recreates bm_staging
#   MAJADU_AUDIT_DSN            belongs to bm2_audit_prune and its own unit
#
# Same value as MAJADU_PG_DSN in majadu-prod.env and majadu-tools.env. The three
# files name the same role on purpose. When bm2_app's password rotates, all three
# are edited in the same step; deploy-vps.sh already fails a prod env that
# carries an owner or ETL DSN, and step 2 of the RLS release adds the mirror
# check for this file.
#
# This is the only variable in the file. The three tools read MAJADU_PG_DSN
# through dsnOrFail (shared/platform-lib/cli.nim:22) and nothing else from the
# environment: the MAJADU_DB_* timeouts belong to the API process edge
# (apps/api/src/main.nim:156), not to openDb's own defaults.
MAJADU_PG_DSN=postgres://bm2_app:CHANGE_ME@qouver-postgres:5432/bm2
